From 48eb353da9a53c743bc1113c4eac7bd9234a9f97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:37:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, settings: tool, terminal and edit cards in three
 states
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.44 (ask 68). A card was open or closed, and a closed
terminal card still showed its whole command, wrapped, so a long command took
several lines. A card now has three states, and a click on its chevron steps through
them:

- collapsed: one line -- the icon and the start of the command or title, cut
  with `…` where the card ends; a multi-line command shows its first line and
  ` …`. The label cuts it, never the stored command: the copy button copies it
  whole.
- minimized: the whole command or title, wrapped; no output. A title is put in
  a block as wide as the header (wrap_title): as a flex item it would be as
  wide as its text and the header would clip it -- the Xvfb proof caught that.
- maximized: the command or title and the content (terminal output, diff,
  input and output) -- what "expanded" was.

A card with nothing to maximize steps between the first two. A card waiting
for confirmation still always shows its content.

Each kind has its own default (operator, 2026-11-16): new settings
agent.terminal_card_default, agent.edit_card_default and
agent.tool_card_default (collapsed | minimized | maximized), on the Settings
page beside Expand Terminal/Edit Card. Until one is set each kind keeps its
old look: upstream's expand_terminal_card and expand_edit_card choose
maximized; otherwise a terminal shows its whole command and an edit or any
other tool its one-line title. A kind's own setting wins over expand_*_card.
The agent menu's "Terminals Minimized by Default" toggle (0090, §6.17)
becomes three submenus -- Terminal Cards, Tool Cards, Edit Cards -- each with
Collapsed, Minimized and Maximized; choosing one for a terminal or an edit
also writes expand_*_card (on for maximized), so the Settings page and the
menu never disagree. terminals_minimized.rs goes; tool_card_display.rs holds
the rules.

EntryViewState's expanded set becomes a map to the state, with no entry
meaning the kind's default. expand/collapse/toggle keep their meaning for
every upstream caller: expand is maximized, collapse is minimized
(explicitly, so a kind that defaults to maximized does not reopen a terminal
moved to the background), toggle is a subagent card's two states.

Tests: tool_card_display_tests.rs (defaults with and without a choice, the
cycle, the menu keeping expand_*_card in step), thread_view/
tool_card_state_tests.rs (the collapsed line) and conversation_view/tests/
tool_card_display_tests.rs (the thread view: a tool card's three states,
the kind's setting as default, an edit kind's choice winning over
expand_edit_card). Red seen: with the explicit choice ignored and the cycle
never reaching maximized, exactly the five tests on those rules failed.

